From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gennro <gennro2004@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 07:01:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 51/57] panvk: fail pipelines with tessellation shaders
 (06n-arch)

tessellationShader isn't advertised, but DXVK still exposes feature
level 11_0 and passes the hull and domain shaders a game uses to the
driver as tessellation control and evaluation stages. The VS/FS backend
doesn't handle their intrinsics (load_invocation_id,
load_per_vertex_input) and then crashes in bi_extract(), taking the
game down with it: Fallout 4 crashes this way loading a save.

Fail such pipelines the way 0017 fails an unfoldable geometry shader.
DXVK logs the failure and skips the draws that use it, so tessellated
geometry is missing but the game runs.

Not for upstream: a local stopgap until PanVK has tessellation.
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c | 17 +++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
index 5cfd6661c15..5b7ddcf63a6 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_vX_shader.c
@@ -2634,6 +2634,23 @@ compile_shaders(struct vk_device *vk_dev, uint32_t shader_count,
    VkResult result;
    int32_t i;
 
+   /* 06n-arch DXVK hack: tessellationShader isn't advertised, but DXVK
+    * still exposes feature level 11_0 and compiles the hull/domain shaders
+    * games give it (Fallout 4). The VS/FS backend crashes on their
+    * intrinsics, so fail the pipeline; DXVK then skips the draws that use it.
+    */
+   for (i = 0; i < shader_count; i++) {
+      if (infos[i].stage == MESA_SHADER_TESS_CTRL ||
+          infos[i].stage == MESA_SHADER_TESS_EVAL) {
+         mesa_logw_once("panvk: tessellation shaders are not implemented, "
+                        "failing the pipeline (06n-arch DXVK hack)");
+         for (int32_t j = 0; j < shader_count; j++)
+            ralloc_free(infos[j].nir);
+         memset(shaders_out, 0, shader_count * sizeof(*shaders_out));
+         return vk_error(dev, VK_ERROR_UNKNOWN);
+      }
+   }
+
    /* 06n-arch: fold pass-through GSes compiled together with their VS into
     * the VS (see analyze_passthrough_gs()), which is much cheaper than
     * running the GS. Any other GS is compiled for the compute emulation
